### Get Current User Profile - GET /auth/me
# Returns the authenticated user's profile
GET http://localhost:5000/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### Get Current User Profile - No Token (should fail with 401)
GET http://localhost:5000/auth/me
Accept: application/json

###

### Get Current User Profile - Invalid Token (should fail with 401)
GET http://localhost:5000/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer invalid.jwt.token

###

### Get Current User Profile - Malformed Authorization Header (should fail)
GET http://localhost:5000/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: InvalidHeader

###

### Get All Users - GET /auth/users
# Returns a list of all users (may require admin privileges)
GET http://localhost:5000/auth/users
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### Get All Users - No Token (should fail with 401)
GET http://localhost:5000/auth/users
Accept: application/json

###

### Get All Users - Invalid Token (should fail with 401)
GET http://localhost:5000/auth/users
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer invalid.jwt.token

###

# ============================================
# SWAGGER/OPENAPI DOCUMENTATION
# ============================================

### Access Swagger UI Documentation
# Open this URL in browser: http://localhost:5000/api-docs

### Get OpenAPI JSON Specification
GET http://localhost:5000/api-docs-json
Accept: application/json

###

# ============================================
# EDGE CASES & SPECIAL CHARACTERS
# ============================================

### Register User - Name with Special Characters
POST http://localhost:5000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "José María García-López",
  "email": "jose.maria@example.com",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

###

### Register User - Email with Plus Sign
POST http://localhost:5000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test Plus",
  "email": "test+alias@example.com",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

###

### Register User - Very Long Name
POST http://localhost:5000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "This Is A Very Long Name That Might Exceed Some Database Limits Or Cause Issues",
  "email": "longname@example.com",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

###

### Register User - Empty Strings (should fail validation)
POST http://localhost:5000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "",
  "email": "",
  "password": ""
}

###

### Register User - Whitespace Only Name (edge case)
POST http://localhost:5000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "   ",
  "email": "whitespace@example.com",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

###

# ============================================
# CONTENT-TYPE VARIATIONS
# ============================================

### Login with Wrong Content-Type (should fail or behave unexpectedly)
POST http://localhost:5000/auth/login
Content-Type: text/plain

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

###

### Login without Content-Type Header
POST http://localhost:5000/auth/login

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

###

# ============================================
# HTTP METHOD VARIATIONS
# ============================================

### Try GET on Login Endpoint (should return 404 or 405)
GET http://localhost:5000/auth/login
Accept: application/json

###

### Try POST on Health Check (should return 404 or 405)
POST http://localhost:5000/
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### Try PUT on Register (should return 404 or 405)
PUT http://localhost:5000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test User",
  "email": "put@example.com",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

###

### Try DELETE on Me Endpoint (should return 404 or 405)
DELETE http://localhost:5000/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

# ============================================
# NON-EXISTENT ROUTES
# ============================================

### Non-existent Route
GET http://localhost:5000/non-existent-route
Accept: application/json

###

### Non-existent Auth Sub-route
GET http://localhost:5000/auth/non-existent
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

